{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1168587-rite-of-becoming-doubt","id":1168587,"title":"Rite of Becoming [Doubt]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-18T12:18:02-08:00","id":1168587,"title":"Rite of Becoming [Doubt]","content":"The methods for entering the deep umbra described in the umbra book are very interesting, but the level 2 ritual (corebook) drew my attention. Everything seemed so easy. until...<br /> <br /> &quot;This rite is cast only in an Anchorhead domain.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where do I find this Anchorhead domain? What does he look like? With the ritual does the garou travel body and spirit, or just spirit? Where do I find information about Anchorhead domains?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23580-baskin","name":"Baskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T15:42:04-08:00","id":1168654,"title":"","content":"Anchorheads are gates in the Horizon, the barrier between the Near Umbra and the Deep Umbra, and every one of them is protected by a powerful Incarna with the task of keeping out everything dangerous that attemps to enter. The Horizon overlaps with the Asteroid belt (so quite far away from the Earth realm) and it's so thick that the only way to move across it is through the Anchorheads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T16:19:49-08:00","id":1168664,"title":"","content":"W20 has the basic information on Anchorheads, though perhaps unsurprisingly W20 Umbra the Velvet Shadow goes into more detail, including how they form, sample Anchorheads, suggestions for ones in places besides the Astral Realm (which has the most and the most 'standard' ones) and who might be guarding them, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T16:24:42-08:00","id":1168666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1168587-rite-of-becoming-doubt?p=1168654#post1168654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anchorheads are gates in the Horizon, the barrier between the Near Umbra and the Deep Umbra, and every one of them is protected by a powerful Incarna with the task of keeping out everything dangerous that attemps to enter. The Horizon overlaps with the Asteroid belt (so quite far away from the Earth realm) and it's so thick that the only way to move across it is through the Anchorheads.</div> </div> </div> </div>NB: Werewolf pays no attention to the Horizon of Mage. The Membrane mentioned in the Rite of Becoming is not really the same thing, since belief doesn't have anywhere near the punch in W:tA that it does in M:tA, and also it's not coterminus with the asteroid belt of the solar system, since that's a real, physical location in Werewolf and not part of the Umbra (as distinguished from the Aetherial Realm)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T04:35:09-08:00","id":1168764,"title":"","content":"So, there are two different but unrelated barriers separating the near Umbra from the Deep one? =P No, I think not. Sure, we coould talk about it in an endless crossover argument but let's just not.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are differences between how the Umbra is perceived by werewolves and how mages experience it, but while I do agree that the geographical locations of Umbral constructs don't matter much in Werewolf I wouldn't write them off so completely. Anyway, the important thing for the OP is that Anchorheads are holes in the Membrane, they're guarded and each one has a specific theme. I'd suggest looking at Velvet Shadow for further informations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T12:10:24-08:00","id":1168878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1168587-rite-of-becoming-doubt?p=1168764#post1168764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there are two different but unrelated barriers separating the near Umbra from the Deep one? =P No, I think not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Deep Umbra? Because Mages often seem to go to some crazy place that others don't, which has basically no intersection with anything else in any other WoD games, as it doesn't even match up with the Werewolf Deep Umbra unless you're playing a Dreamspeaker, and possibly not even then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, we coould talk about it in an endless crossover argument but let's just not. </div> </div> </div>There is no crossover argument because, again, you have to pick one when it comes to Mage and Werewolf. The two will not mix well when it comes to cosmology, and the wishy-washy nature of Mage in attempting to explain things is a cosmology that only gets supported in Mage books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, there are differences between how the Umbra is perceived by werewolves and how mages experience it, but while I do agree that the geographical locations of Umbral constructs don't matter much in Werewolf I wouldn't write them off so completely. </div> </div> </div>I would. The assumptions of Werewolf and Wraith produce a Dark Umbra that's an entirely different location from the Astral, Middle and what have you, not just some kind of filter on a general Umbra. Also, space, all of space, is physical just like the Earth, no matter how far you happen to be from Earth. The differences were substantial enough that there was a sidebar in the Mokole book about it to remind readers that the Werewolf Deep Umbra in that edition was what Mages referred to as the High Umbra, and the Mage's Deep Umbra was simply just outer space, because Werewolf did not, and still does not, utilize concepts of Mage like Dreamshells or Horizons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, the important thing for the OP is that Anchorheads are holes in the Membrane, they're guarded and each one has a specific theme. I'd suggest looking at Velvet Shadow for further informations. </div> </div> </div>Also, that's specifically the W20 Umbra book or Umbra Revised that people should consult. The first edition book might not be quite as helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}